From: J7 Prime bring-up
Subject: j7prime: respect active-low LCD backlight enable

The on7xelte panel DTS declares GPD3-5 as GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW. Drive the pin
low to illuminate the panel and high to switch the backlight off. The
previous 0319 polarity was reversed, which left the backlight dark on wake.

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -241,1 +241,1 @@
-/* TOP pinctrl: GPD3 begins at +0x140; LCD_BL_EN is active-high GPD3-5. */
+/* TOP pinctrl: GPD3 begins at +0x140; LCD_BL_EN is active-low GPD3-5. */
@@ -270,9 +270,9 @@ j7_fb_backlight(bool enabled)
 	volatile uint32_t *con = (volatile uint32_t *)(j7_fb_top_pins + 0x140);
 	volatile uint32_t *dat = (volatile uint32_t *)(j7_fb_top_pins + 0x144);
 	uint32_t c = *con;
 	uint32_t d = *dat;
 	c = (c & ~(0xfu << 20)) | (1u << 20); /* GPD3-5 output */
-	d = enabled ? (d | (1u << 5)) : (d & ~(1u << 5));
+	d = enabled ? (d & ~(1u << 5)) : (d | (1u << 5));
 	*con = c;
 	__asm__ volatile("dmb oshst" ::: "memory");
 	*dat = d;
